: "37dda141", "chg": 68095, "ps": 15, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 2448, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 03:47", "ord": 15, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68095/15/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#2448", "txt": "This isn't a bug, but the return convention is the opposite of the one its neighbours use. find_check_layout(), find_check_foreign(), find_check_stripe_size() and find_value_cmp() ", "sub": "find on the scan record"}, {"id": "48bdbc10", "chg": 68156, "ps": 14, "file": "lustreapi_scan_backend.h", "path": "lustre/utils/lustreapi_scan_backend.h", "line": 125, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 04:06", "ord": 16, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68156/14/lustre/utils/lustreapi_scan_backend.h#125", "txt": "Is \"nothing lies at or beyond this chunk\" what *done means to the core? scan_ldiskfs_scan_chunk() sets it before it scans anything, on the chunk whose end_ino reaches s_inodes_coun", "sub": "ldiskfs target scan"}, {"id": "ac3c6de6", "chg": 68156, "ps": 14, "file": "libscan_ldiskfs.c", "path": "lustre/utils/libscan_ldiskfs.c", "line": 44, "sev": "typo", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 04:06", "ord": 17, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68156/14/lustre/utils/libscan_ldiskfs.c#44", "txt": "enum llapi_scan_xattr has six entries, so scan_want_xattr() can ask for five beyond trusted.lma -- LOV, LMV, SOM, LINK and HSM -- not four. The count reads as if trusted.hsm were n", "sub": "ldiskfs target scan"}, {"id": "af0db1f1", "chg": 68156, "ps": 14, "file": "llapi_scan_namespace.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_namespace.3", "line": 270, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 04:06", "ord": 18, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68156/14/Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_namespace.3#270", "txt": "The commit message says this page \"gains the pointer to this page\", but SEE ALSO further down still lists only lfs-find(1), llapi_layout_get_by_xattr(3) and lustreapi(7). llapi_sca", "sub": "ldiskfs target scan"}, {"id": "c83c49c3", "chg": 68156, "ps": 14, "file": "lustreapi.h", "path": "include/lustre/lustreapi.h", "line": 714, "sev": "suggestion", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 04:06", "ord": 19, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68156/14/include/lustre/lustreapi.h#714", "txt": "The invariant is stated unconditionally, but sum(ss_class) is taken over LLAPI_SCAN_CLS_MAX, which is the caller's compiled-in value. This structure is size-versioned like the rest", "sub": "ldiskfs target scan"}, {"id": "fab8ec72", "chg": 68156, "ps": 14, "file": "llapi_scan_namespace.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_namespace.3", "line": 48, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 04:06", "ord": 20, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68156/14/Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_namespace.3#48", "txt": "This paragraph walks struct llapi_scan_param field by field -- sp_size, sp_max_depth, sp_thread_count, sp_flags, sp_padding, then sp_want and sp_filter below -- and the patch adds ", "sub": "ldiskfs target scan"}, {"id": "7b88705b", "chg": 68159, "ps": 14, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3206, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 05:02", "ord": 21, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68159/14/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3206", "txt": "This floor is sizeof(struct lov_user_md_v1), 32 bytes, and it runs before the magic is looked at -- so the foreign arm below, whose own floor is offsetof(struct lov_foreign_md, lfm", "sub": "find over a device scan"}, {"id": "8ac2878f", "chg": 68159, "ps": 14, "file": "llapi_find_device.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_find_device.3", "line": 92, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 05:02", "ord": 22, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68159/14/Documentation/man3/llapi_find_device.3#92", "txt": "llapi_find_device() returns llapi_scan_device()'s value unchanged, so a caller also sees -ENOPKG (backend refused the target) and -EIO, neither of which is listed, and -ENOTSUP for", "sub": "find over a device scan"}, {"id": "de93d86e", "chg": 68159, "ps": 14, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3521, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 05:02", "ord": 23, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68159/14/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3521", "txt": "The comment names \"a size or a time\", but only the size and the block count end up counted. With fc_lustre_fs 0, find_decide() computes", "sub": "find over a device scan"}, {"id": "53bb1a2b", "chg": 68417, "ps": 6, "file": "Makefile.am", "path": "Documentation/man3/Makefile.am", "line": 29, "sev": "suggestion", "st": "nochange", "t": "2026-09-01 06:30", "ord": 24, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68417/6/Documentation/man3/Makefile.am#29", "txt": "Documentation/man7/lustreapi.7 indexes the library's entry points by topic, and neither llapi_find_since() nor the llapi_scan_*/llapi_find_device() pages the earlier patches in thi", "sub": "find --since"}, {"id": "cf96d311", "chg": 68417, "ps": 6, "file": "lfs_find_parse.c", "path": "lustre/utils/lfs_find_parse.c", "line": 902, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 06:30", "ord": 25, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68417/6/lustre/utils/lfs_find_parse.c#902", "txt": "This table and the one -newerXt uses further down in the same file now accept different time spellings, and nothing says so. --since adds the ISO \"T\" forms but drops \"%H:%M\" and \"%", "sub": "find --since"}, {"id": "eb5939c8", "chg": 68417, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3993, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 06:30", "ord": 26, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68417/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3993", "txt": "The comment says a walk \"would compose dir//name\", but that is what a walk actually prints. param_callback() copies the argument verbatim, trailing slash and all, and llapi_semanti", "sub": "find --since"}, {"id": "fb06db27", "chg": 68417, "ps": 6, "file": "llapi_find_since.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_find_since.3", "line": 102, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 06:30", "ord": 27, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68417/6/Documentation/man3/llapi_find_since.3#102", "txt": "The \"filesystem or mount point cannot be found\" half of this looks like it is -ENODEV rather than -ENOENT. Both lookups end in get_root_path(), which starts at `rc = -ENODEV` and r", "sub": "find --since"}, {"id": "a8944be2", "chg": 68160, "ps": 15, "file": "llapi_find_device.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_find_device.3", "line": 1, "sev": "style", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 06:48", "ord": 28, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68160/15/Documentation/man3/llapi_find_device.3#1", "txt": "Not a bug, but the .TH date stays at 2026-08-20 although this patch changes the page's text and its SEE ALSO list. lfs-find.1 in the same patch gets its date bumped for a strictly ", "sub": "lfind"}, {"id": "065fbc0b", "chg": 68163, "ps": 13, "file": "lustre-build-zfs.m4", "path": "config/lustre-build-zfs.m4", "line": 250, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:13", "ord": 29, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68163/13/config/lustre-build-zfs.m4#250", "txt": "Is the \"Not Found\" half of this condition still reachable? \"[Not Found]\" is only ever assigned to $zfsinc up at line 211, and $zfsinc is no longer one of the candidates the loop wa", "sub": "ZFS backend"}, {"id": "cc416ff2", "chg": 68163, "ps": 13, "file": "llapi_scan_device.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_device.3", "line": 1, "sev": "style", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:13", "ord": 30, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68163/13/Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_device.3#1", "txt": "Not a bug, but the .TH date is still the parent patch's 2026-08-19 while this revision adds a \"Finding a target that is named by label\" subsection and five new ERRORS entries. lfin", "sub": "ZFS backend"}, {"id": "ccf9de29", "chg": 68163, "ps": 13, "file": "liblustreapi_scan_device.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_device.c", "line": 776, "sev": "style", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:13", "ord": 31, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68163/13/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_device.c#776", "txt": "This isn't a bug, but the macro now reads `symbol` and `name` out of the enclosing function while still taking `handle` and `ops` as parameters, so what it touches is no longer vis", "sub": "ZFS backend"}, {"id": "28ece513", "chg": 68415, "ps": 6, "file": "llapi_scan_changelog.3", "path": "Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_changelog.3", "line": 76, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:18", "ord": 32, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68415/6/Documentation/man3/llapi_scan_changelog.3#76", "txt": "For a CL_RENAME, sr_fid is not the object that moved. mdd_rename() passes the destination object as the changelog target:", "sub": "changelog as object stream"}, {"id": "4e135ff9", "chg": 68415, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "line": 798, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:18", "ord": 33, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68415/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c#798", "txt": "This isn't a bug, but ss_seen counts the record that ended the range: the sc_endrec test below runs after the increment, so a scan bounded by sc_endrec reports one more record exam", "sub": "changelog as object stream"}, {"id": "5292db1d", "chg": 68415, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "line": 545, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:18", "ord": 34, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68415/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c#545", "txt": "fid_is_sane() does not reject a CL_MARK, so the comment above and the per-event fallback do not cover it.", "sub": "changelog as object stream"}, {"id": "5441df70", "chg": 68415, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "line": 706, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:18", "ord": 35, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68415/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c#706", "txt": "This size test cannot be false: scl.sc_size was set to sizeof(scl) two lines up, and offsetof(..., sc_stats) is smaller. The comment explains the test as guarding a read past a sho", "sub": "changelog as object stream"}, {"id": "76df3e5e", "chg": 68415, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c", "line": 436, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:18", "ord": 36, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68415/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan_changelog.c#436", "txt": "For a CLF_RENAME record cr_namelen covers both names, not just the target one.", "sub": "changelog as object stream"}, {"id": "0fda8c12", "chg": 68288, "ps": 8, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3099, "sev": "minor", "st": "nochange", "t": "2026-09-01 07:34", "ord": 37, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68288/8/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3099", "txt": "Can this arm run? scan_rec_obj() in liblustreapi_scan_device.c sets sr_valid = LLAPI_SCAN_INO | ... unconditionally for every record it builds, and find_device_cb() is the only cal", "sub": "name a scan's objects"}, {"id": "1d303ab4", "chg": 68288, "ps": 8, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3075, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:34", "ord": 38, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68288/8/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3075", "txt": "\"A FID from another filesystem does not reach here: no FLD range covers its sequence\" does not seem to hold, and the failure mode is a silently wrong answer rather than a missing o", "sub": "name a scan's objects"}, {"id": "6a06b72f", "chg": 68288, "ps": 8, "file": "lfind.8", "path": "Documentation/man8/lfind.8", "line": 130, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:34", "ord": 39, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68288/8/Documentation/man8/lfind.8#130", "txt": "The wrong-filesystem paragraph promises more than the code delivers. \"No sequence of this target lives there\" is not true: FID_SEQ_ROOT and FID_SEQ_DOT_LUSTRE are constants shared ", "sub": "name a scan's objects"}, {"id": "7bb70878", "chg": 68288, "ps": 8, "file": "lfind.8", "path": "Documentation/man8/lfind.8", "line": 8, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:34", "ord": 40, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68288/8/Documentation/man8/lfind.8#8", "txt": "MOUNT ends up in roman and the closing bracket in bold here, unlike DEVICE/NAME/FILTER on the neighbouring lines:", "sub": "name a scan's objects"}, {"id": "ac08f143", "chg": 68288, "ps": 8, "file": "COMMIT_MSG", "path": "COMMIT_MSG", "line": 33, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:34", "ord": 41, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68288/8/COMMIT_MSG#33", "txt": "Is this paragraph right that another filesystem always answers -ENOENT? FID sequences are not unique across filesystems. FID_SEQ_ROOT is a constant (lustre_idl.h: 0x200000007), so ", "sub": "name a scan's objects"}, {"id": "02960867", "chg": 68418, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 2463, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:41", "ord": 42, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68418/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#2463", "txt": "Should a record that carries no name count as undecided rather than be matched against the empty string? find_device_prefilter() returns 2 for exactly this case and its caller bump", "sub": "find --changelog"}, {"id": "3d0299b2", "chg": 68418, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3099, "sev": "style", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:41", "ord": 43, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68418/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3099", "txt": "This isn't a bug, but both arms do the same increment. Hoisting it reads as \"always count, print when the caller asked for a FID\":", "sub": "find --changelog"}, {"id": "4711011a", "chg": 68418, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 4312, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:41", "ord": 44, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68418/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#4312", "txt": "This paragraph and the Return: below still describe --since alone. Under --changelog the object is not verified through the mount, the answer is not a subset of the plain search (a", "sub": "find --changelog"}, {"id": "52f04fea", "chg": 68418, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 4218, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 07:41", "ord": 45, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68418/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#4218", "txt": "Should -uid/-gid and --mdt-count/--mdt-hash be in this list too? find_changelog_supported() returns 0 as soon as fp_resolve is set, so all four get past the refusal on the strength", "sub": "find --changelog"}, {"id": "11d9a284", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3894, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 46, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3894", "txt": "When the cookie sits directly in the root directory, `tmp` is \"/<name>.new\", `sep` points at index 0, and `*sep = '\\0'` leaves `tmp` empty -- so `open(\"\", O_RDONLY | O_DIRECTORY)` ", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "1413b6e2", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 4638, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 47, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#4638", "txt": "The kernel-doc still says the search arrives \"with fp_since_kind set\", and the Return: block lists only the two old -EINVAL cases. fp_since_cookie now selects this path on its own,", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "4a4f68e7", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3989, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 48, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3989", "txt": "`cookie` cannot be NULL here -- the only call site is inside `if (param->fp_since_cookie != NULL)` and passes that same pointer -- and the -ESTALE message below hands `cookie` to %", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "852a7170", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 4560, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 49, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#4560", "txt": "The comment says the index is taken \"whether or not the object is a match\", but the update sits below the `sr_valid & LLAPI_SCAN_FID` gate a few lines up, so a record with no targe", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "8656cfdd", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "COMMIT_MSG", "path": "COMMIT_MSG", "line": 63, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 50, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/COMMIT_MSG#63", "txt": "The find_device_supported() hunk isn't accounted for anywhere in the body. It does two things: it adds `--since-cookie` to the refusal, which belongs here, and it adds `--changelog", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "8c3c160f", "chg": 68419, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_pfind.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c", "line": 3832, "sev": "style", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:16", "ord": 51, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68419/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_pfind.c#3832", "txt": "This isn't a bug, but there are two comment blocks stacked here with no code between them, which reads as a leftover from an earlier merge of the two. They also disagree slightly -", "sub": "find --since-cookie"}, {"id": "21d7a451", "chg": 68420, "ps": 6, "file": "sanity.sh", "path": "lustre/tests/sanity.sh", "line": 22792, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:35", "ord": 52, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68420/6/lustre/tests/sanity.sh#22792", "txt": "These two run against the cookie the block above has just made stale, so both commands fail with ESTALE before the refusal they are aiming at is reached.", "sub": "sanity cases"}, {"id": "88bfadaf", "chg": 68420, "ps": 6, "file": "sanity.sh", "path": "lustre/tests/sanity.sh", "line": 22564, "sev": "suggestion", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:35", "ord": 53, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68420/6/lustre/tests/sanity.sh#22564", "txt": "--since takes four spellings and only two of them are covered here: a duration, and a bare index in the refusal arm below. A timestamp (--since 2026-08-25T18:00), the explicit epoc", "sub": "sanity cases"}, {"id": "acb1618c", "chg": 68420, "ps": 6, "file": "lfs-find.1", "path": "Documentation/man1/lfs-find.1", "line": 784, "sev": "unlabelled", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:35", "ord": 54, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68420/6/Documentation/man1/lfs-find.1#784", "txt": "-type is neither in this refusal list nor always answerable, and the page does not say so.", "sub": "sanity cases"}, {"id": "1f0fff10", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c", "line": 676, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 55, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c#676", "txt": "linkno is fixed at 0, so a hardlinked object is gathered at whichever link the MDT lists first. llapi_scan_rec_path()'s kernel-doc says so (\"A hardlinked object has one pathname pe", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "466cb29f", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c", "line": 825, "sev": "defect", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 56, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c#825", "txt": "The open runs whatever sp_want asked for, but scan_rec_gather() returns at its first line when nothing in LLAPI_SCAN_MDT_MASK is set:", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "4ae6a0e5", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "lustreapi_internal.h", "path": "lustre/utils/lustreapi_internal.h", "line": 363, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 57, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/lustreapi_internal.h#363", "txt": "llapi_scan_device() does not widen 0 the same way:", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "7cc6358d", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c", "line": 746, "sev": "suggestion", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 58, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c#746", "txt": "common_param_init() is a per-scan cost for the other entry points - llapi_find_with_cb() and llapi_find_device() each call it once - but it lands per object here. It calloc()s offs", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "9ae545d1", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c", "line": 850, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 59, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c#850", "txt": "This is skipped in the same case the open above is wasted in. With sp_want holding nothing from LLAPI_SCAN_MDT_MASK, scan_rec_gather() returns before scan_rec_mdt() runs, LLAPI_SCA", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "db00c964", "chg": 68416, "ps": 6, "file": "liblustreapi_scan.c", "path": "lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c", "line": 727, "sev": "suggestion", "st": "nochange", "t": "2026-09-01 08:39", "ord": 60, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68416/6/lustre/utils/liblustreapi_scan.c#727", "txt": "llapi_scan_rec_path() a hundred lines below does these same three steps - llapi_fid2path_at(), skip the leading slashes, compose `<mnt>/<rel>` with the root special case - and the ", "sub": "scan record for one FID"}, {"id": "b8772d34", "chg": 68413, "ps": 5, "file": "mdd_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/mdd/mdd_changelog.c", "line": 80, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 09:18", "ord": 61, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68413/5/lustre/mdd/mdd_changelog.c#80", "txt": "The count here is the destination's 30 bytes, while cur_name is 16. Under the premise the comment above states - no guaranteed NUL inside cur_name - this reads on into cur_padding2", "sub": "mdd changelog user lookup"}, {"id": "c9bda014", "chg": 68413, "ps": 5, "file": "mdd_changelog.c", "path": "lustre/mdd/mdd_changelog.c", "line": 51, "sev": "minor", "st": "addressed", "t": "2026-09-01 09:18", "ord": 62, "url": "https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68413/5/lustre/mdd/mdd_changelog.c#51", "txt": "Is LU-19296 the right boundary here? 5b85a4eb7510 only added this callback and the MDT/MDC plumbing; it did not touch how the record is written.", "sub": "mdd changelog user lookup"}]